# Goobers runtime state — belt-and-suspenders only.
#
# The runtime instance should be materialized OUTSIDE this repo (see README.md);
# nothing generated at runtime is needed here. These patterns are deliberately
# specific so they can NEVER shadow the checked-in config source
# (manifest.yaml, gaggles/**/*.yaml, instructions.md, *.example, README.md).

# Runtime instance-root files (a materialized instance writes these)
/instance.yaml
/telemetry.db
/telemetry.db-shm
/telemetry.db-wal

# Runtime directories: top-level runs/workcopies aliases + scheduler ledger
/runs/
/workcopies/
/scheduler/

# Per-gaggle runtime state — keeps gaggle.yaml, goobers/, and workflows/ tracked
gaggles/*/runs/
gaggles/*/workcopies/
gaggles/*/.runs.*

# NOTE: intentionally NOT ignoring `config/`. Our config source is laid out flat
# (manifest.yaml + gaggles/ at the root of this directory, like Goobers'
# config-examples/ and selfhost/). A materialized instance's `config/` is a copy
# that belongs OUTSIDE the repo. If you ever adopt the concepts-doc layout that
# nests definitions under config/, remove this note — do NOT add `config/` here,
# or you will silently hide committed config.
